<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit Cap for Shadow Priests</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 15% or 5100 Hit Rating. Your priority is to reach these with any combination of Hit, Expertise, and Spirit, given that we have <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=47573/spiritual-precision">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_divinespirit.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spiritual Precision</span></a>. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 15% Hit, your spell hits will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This effectively means your abilities will never miss.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Shadow Priests</span></h2>Shadow Priest has always been a class that feels better with gear. The more Haste you have, the more fun your character is to play. We generally want to aim for Haste and Intellect on our Gems. Whether you want to focus on pure Haste-oriented gems or Intellect-oriented gems, you should sim the difference in any given gear combination.<br/>
<br/>Gems are also a great place to grab any Hit and Spirit that we may be missing.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95347/sinister-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Sinister Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sinister Primal Diamond</span></a> or <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76885/burning-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Burning Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Burning Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76694/brilliant-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
