<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Shadow Priests</span></h2>Every profession is viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic, all giving similar power benefits in a variety of implementations. Our preferred choice is Engineering, due to the utility of effects and early craftable armor, and Tailoring, due to the multiplicative scaling of the embroidery buffs. Other professions provide values that usually average out to about 320 Intellect in power level, but are overshadowed by our two main choices. Our only lackluster choices are the Gathering professions, as their benefits are minuscule to non-existent. Herbalism is the only one worth mentioning with its Haste buff; however, it is overshadowed by the added Intellect from the other professions.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Shadow Priests</h4>Engineering brings with it the following:<br/>
<br/>
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> which you can apply to your Glove slot, giving you a 1920 Intellect buff that lasts for 10 seconds on a 1-minute cooldown. This averages out to about 320 Intellect as long as you use it whenever it is available.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=54793/frag-belt">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frag Belt</span></a>, which can be applied to the Waist slot, allowing you to deal some damage off the global cooldown occasionally.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Shadow Priests</h4>Tailoring gives embroideries that you will definitely get some use out of via <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125482/darkglow-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkglow Embroidery</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142173/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a>.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_chest_cloth_challengepriest_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Shadow Priests</span></h3>Crafted items are no longer restricted by your Profession option, except for Engineering, so this allows us to equip Tailoring items without Tailoring if we need to.<br/>
